Relevant columns and their possible roles  

• `event_date`: filter events to September 2018; turn the yyyymmdd string into DATE and use it to calculate the number‑of‑days gap between two events.  
• `event_name`: pick only the events we care about:  
  – `first_open` (“first time a user opened the app”)  
  – `app_remove` (“uninstall”)  
  – `app_exception` (“crash”)  
• `user_pseudo_id`: join the three event types together user‑by‑user and keep them unique.  
• `event_timestamp`: (optional) finer ordering when two events share the same calendar date.  
No other columns are strictly required for the requested calculation.  

Typical filters / conditions you will see below  

```
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '20180901' AND '20180930'              -- only September ’18
      AND event_name = 'first_open'                                 -- or app_remove, …  
```

